-- 2026-11-21 (Logan): catch-up records for ve-front-of-house, Nov 13 decisions not yet in the playbook. Add-only (Sean, 2026-11-21: "make sure
-- that whatever wasn't captured is captured, as long as it doesn't overwrite any new things"). Nothing existing is updated. Safe to run twice.
insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, source, kind, body)
select 've-front-of-house', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', 'text', 'decision', x.body
from (values
 ('ve-front-of-house: photographers come from our ecosystem (Sean, 2026-11-13). "Why aren''t we just reaching out to content creators? I want to stay within our ecosystem. We should be more of a referral network than going to these big companies... Let''s show them exactly what we want and help them become better food photographers... we could reach out to colleges... Let''s create the demand." The cold photographer list (C&I Studios, Miami Profile, Riguel Dorta, Jason Varney, Philly Vegans) was retired UNSENT: campaign photographer-bench-2026-email finished, DMs closed, pb-* links off (migration 20261113_photographer_bench_retire_cold_list.sql). The two paid jobs stay open on the Gig Board (Fort Lauderdale 724b97fa, Philadelphia 25c1cc7f; $75 paid trial; applications close Dec 4). Order: the Food Photographer Guide first, then the job rewritten to start from it, then outreach to our own creators and Ambassadors, members, then colleges.'),
 ('ve-front-of-house: OUTREACH IS THE LAST STEP (Sean, 2026-11-13: "I don''t even know what we''re sending to them. Did we lock it in? Let''s finish it before we start talking about outreach. Outreach should be the last thing we do."). Postmortem: repeat of canon-sean-one-next-step; rule added to vegansexplore-com CLAUDE.md and canon-sean-one-next-step body.outreach_last (migration 20261113_canon_outreach_last.sql).'),
 ('ve-front-of-house: THE FOOD PHOTOGRAPHER GUIDE. Outline LOCKED by Sean 2026-11-13 ("lock it, yes"): Overview, What good looks like, Your phone, Your camera, Light and when to shoot, The two angles, Plating and drinks, The space and the people, Delivering, Get paid. Built the same day from the Welcome Guide (guides/food-photographer-guide.html, guide-scripts/food-photographer-guide.js, pictures public/guides/food-photo/, VE main 7c44acb); Sean: "Yeah, it looks good." Since moved onto the Handbook template and option C in playbook ve-holiday-guide (2026-11-17/18, approved there); this record does not change that. STILL OPEN, waiting on Sean: (1) yes to the 10 lesson pictures, Kai doing each page''s lesson with the locked scene recipe (cafe table with camera; comparing printed dish photos; phone over a plate with grid; camera on tripod; window side light with a white card; overhead and 45 degree; wiping a rim and a backlit drink; outside a cafe at dusk; laptop into the shot list; handshake with an owner), Green Leaf photos kept only where they are the result. Sean asked for "actual images that reflect what''s there". (2) Pay per shoot for photographers (Logan recommends a flat $150 per 8-dish shoot; the shop sells it at $250). Then: remove the Preview banner, record Kai''s lines after Sean approves them, rewrite the job, outreach last.')
) x(body)
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records p where p.slug = 've-front-of-house' and p.body = x.body);

